<title>MEXICO: Mexico lowers jet fuel prices-Petroleos Mexicanos.</title>
<headline>Mexico lowers jet fuel prices-Petroleos Mexicanos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's state-owned oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) said Monday it will lower jet fuel prices on Tuesday to 1,801.59 pesos per cubic meter from 1,928.81 pesos per cubic meter.</p>
<p>Pemex said in a press statement that jet fuel prices have risen from 1,253.50 pesos since the beginning of 1996. The company regularly adjusts jet fuel prices according to international prices.</p>
<p>--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903</p>
</text>
